### TASK-260715-1ozsb6_inputs.md
> libssh2 adapter requirements + neutral-seam fit

Implement the libssh2 CANDIDATE adapter — a SSHTransport implementation satisfying the candidate-neutral contract (TASK-260720-100wu6 in Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift), backed by libssh2. Package libssh2 (pinned per TASK-260715-28ok1k: commit a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719, BSD-3-Clause; OpenSSL 3.5.7 backend, Apache-2.0) as a static XCFramework binaryTarget via the TASK-260715-1g9cyt native seam + rebuild hook (checksum-verify pinned source; ADR-019). Live behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary as a NAMED adapter module (libssh2/OpenSSL imported ONLY here; NOT in ReluxTunnelCore proper — make validate-core enforces). KEY FIT (why libssh2 suits the neutral seam where NIOSSH did not): drive libssh2 over the injected neutral SSHTCPConnection (readySome/readSome/writeSome/close) using libssh2 CUSTOM TRANSPORT send/recv callbacks (libssh2_session_callback_set) in NONBLOCKING mode (EAGAIN) — no socket/descriptor ownership needed, so the injected/fakeable connector (E-INJECTION) works. IMPLEMENT the full contract: connect + MANDATORY pre-auth host-key verification (libssh2 hostkey + SHA256 fingerprint to injected policy before credential lookup; changed-key stop); public-key auth via an EXTERNAL SIGNER (libssh2_userauth_publickey sign-callback — private key NEVER exported, stays with the caller); openDirectTCPIP (libssh2_channel_direct_tcpip_ex); openExecChannel (exec); upload via exec-stdin (NO SFTP); PER-CHANNEL window via libssh2_channel_open_ex(window_size)+window_read_ex+receive_window_adjust2 with CONSUMER-DRIVEN credit (return credit only after the API read consumes bytes — libssh2 lets the adapter own credit return, satisfying contract section 9 backpressure and maximumBufferedReadBytes); client REKEY by byte/time threshold scheduled by the adapter (libssh2 has no auto-rekey threshold — see audit); keepalive (libssh2_keepalive) with RTT; bounded IO/EOF/reset/cancel/close; error taxonomy; privacy-safe metrics; report exact negotiated KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC. UNIT-TEST driven over an in-memory/loopback byte seam (no live SSH fixtures — those are 39xz9g; cross-engine conformance is 2d3g5e; functional/scale is 1u2vpc, P0-gated). This is a CANDIDATE, not the selection (1gjxer). Build+test via swift build/test on macOS. If a contract clause genuinely cannot be satisfied by libssh2 public API, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact gap (that would signal a contract revision, a bigger decision) — do not force-fit.




## Board CLI Reference

You have access to `task-board` CLI for managing your work. All writes use the `m` (mutation DSL) subcommand:

```bash
# The FIRST/LAST sections above define your role-default lifecycle commands.
# Use explicit status changes when the task flow requires it.
task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, status=analysis)'       # analyst-style work
task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, status=development)'    # implementation / testing work
task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, status=reviewing)'      # reviewer handoff
task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, status=blocked)'        # when blocked
task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, status=to-review)'      # when your work is ready for review

# Track progress with checklist
task-board m 'check_item(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, item=1)'                        # check item N
task-board m 'add_checklist_item(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, text="Write tests")'    # add checklist item

# Add notes about your progress, decisions, blockers, or review findings
task-board m 'set_notes(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, text="your note here")'

# Save short text directly as outcome resources
task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260715-1ozsb6, name=TASK-260715-1ozsb6_results.md, content="...", type=outcome, description="Description")'

