218:## libssh2 source findings
219-
220-### Windowing and direct-tcpip
221-
222:[`include/libssh2.h`](https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/blob/a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719/include/libssh2.h#L787)
223:defines the default channel window as 2 MiB and publicly exposes
224:`libssh2_channel_open_ex`, `libssh2_channel_window_read_ex`, and
225:`libssh2_channel_receive_window_adjust2`. The generic open API accepts initial
226:window and packet size. Source comments place receive-window maintenance on the
227-caller, which permits a bounded-credit policy.
228-
229-The convenience
230:[`libssh2_channel_direct_tcpip_ex`](https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/blob/a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719/src/channel.c#L407)
231-calls the internal open path with the 2 MiB default. A custom size therefore
232:requires generic `libssh2_channel_open_ex` with channel type `direct-tcpip` and
233-the RFC 4254 target/originator payload. E-WINDOW must prove that construction
234-against OpenSSH before the public API is considered sufficient.
235-
236-### Rekey, concurrency, and cancellation
237-
238-Inbound `SSH_MSG_KEXINIT` is recognized in
239:[`src/packet.c`](https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/blob/a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719/src/packet.c#L1336)
240-and calls internal `ssh2_kex_exchange(session, 1, …)`. The symbol is declared in
241:the private header and is not exported from `include/libssh2.h`. No public local
242:rekey call or automatic byte/time threshold was found. This is a confirmed API
243-absence, not merely undocumented behavior.
244-
245-Channel IDs and channel lookup in
246:[`src/channel.c`](https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/blob/a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719/src/channel.c#L54)
247-walk the session channel list. The source has no small fixed channel ceiling,
248-but O(n) lookup/open behavior makes the 500–1,000 target an empirical CPU and
249-memory gate.
250-
251-The nonblocking contract is EAGAIN plus socket block-direction polling. Session
252-operations mutate shared state and have no internal synchronization; one
253:serialized executor per session is required. `libssh2_session_init_ex` can route
254:libssh2 allocations through accounting hooks, but OpenSSL's internal allocations
255-remain separate. Cancellation has no token/API and must coordinate channel EOF,
256-close/free, socket shutdown, and session teardown without re-entering a session.
257-
258-### Algorithms with the pinned backend
259-
260-OpenSSL 3.5.7 enables Ed25519, ECDSA, RSA-SHA2, AES-GCM, AES-CTR, and the current
261:ML-KEM implementations used by the selected libssh2 commit. At this source the
262-default KEX list starts with `mlkem768x25519-sha256`,
263-`mlkem768nistp256-sha256`, and `mlkem1024nistp384-sha384` when available, then
264-Curve25519, ECDH, and DH variants. The default host-key list covers Ed25519,
265-ECDSA, and RSA-SHA2, including supported OpenSSH certificate variants. Ciphers
266-include ChaCha20-Poly1305, AES-GCM, AES-CTR, and optional legacy modes.
267-
268-The pinned build disables RSA-SHA1 and AES-CBC. The adapter must use method
269-preferences to exclude SHA-1/group1 KEX and HMAC-SHA1 while retaining the
--
287-  but it remains part of the dependency baseline.
