343-## Apple integration and binary risk
344-
345-SwiftNIO SSH follows the reviewable SwiftPM source path required by ADR-019 and
346-shares Swift Crypto/NIO dependencies already expected by the design. Its main
347-integration risks are fork ownership, event-loop correctness, 0.x upstream API
348-movement, and hidden runtime allocation—not native packaging.
349-
350:libssh2 follows the static XCFramework path required by ADR-019. The XCFramework
351-must contain no dylibs, no absolute SDK/library paths, no unsupported slices,
352-and no forbidden extension APIs; must use the project deployment targets; and
353-must provide deterministic source provenance plus the BSD and Apache notices.
354-Static OpenSSL increases code size, native-C attack surface, rebuild burden, and
355-the possibility of two crypto stacks in the extension. These are risks, not
356-measurements. E-SIZE must record per-slice archive size, linked contribution,
357-stripped extension delta, symbols, and notices before selection.
358-
